1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:02,416
Previously on "The 100"...

2
00:00:02,418 --> 00:00:05,677
Thelonious is gone. He
took 12 people, 12 guns.

3
00:00:05,687 --> 00:00:07,287
We're going to the City of Light.

4
00:00:07,289 --> 00:00:09,322
Take this leap of faith
with me, John Murphy,

5
00:00:09,324 --> 00:00:14,561
and let me show you there is so
much more for you... than this.

6
00:00:14,563 --> 00:00:16,329
Quint: Biggest army we've ever had

7
00:00:16,331 --> 00:00:18,198
waits for us to give it a mission.

8
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:21,000
We will, after Bellamy
turns off the acid fog.

9
00:00:21,002 --> 00:00:22,135
If this is an alliance

10
00:00:22,137 --> 00:00:23,870
between the outsiders and the Ark,

11
00:00:23,872 --> 00:00:25,605
we shouldn't take this threat lightly.

12
00:00:25,607 --> 00:00:27,540
There's a war council
meeting happening tonight

13
00:00:27,542 --> 00:00:29,175
and all the leaders are gonna be there.

14
00:00:29,177 --> 00:00:30,143
We're gonna use a missile.

15
00:00:30,145 --> 00:00:31,611
We have to start evacuating.

16
00:00:31,613 --> 00:00:32,745
If we evacuate, they'll know

17
00:00:32,747 --> 00:00:34,380
we have a spy inside their walls.

18
00:00:34,382 --> 00:00:36,349
We slip away. Right now.

19
00:00:36,351 --> 00:00:37,483
Fire.

20
00:00:40,689 --> 00:00:43,122
You knew and you let this happen?

21
00:00:43,124 --> 00:00:45,124
Some of them aren't wearing Hazmat suits.

22
00:00:45,126 --> 00:00:47,660
Means they're cured.
Marrow treatments work.

23
00:00:47,662 --> 00:00:51,798
We started taking them from
the dorm, one at a time.

24
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:55,401
They're not taking anyone else
out of this room without a fight.

25
00:00:55,403 --> 00:00:56,402
Yaah!

26
00:00:56,404 --> 00:00:57,403
Uhh!

27
00:00:57,405 --> 00:00:58,404
Man: Find them.

28
00:00:58,406 --> 00:00:59,572
We're going to hide you.

29
00:00:59,574 --> 00:01:01,074
Not everyone here agrees with Cage.

30
00:01:01,076 --> 00:01:02,675
Come with me. You're safe now.

31
00:01:07,749 --> 00:01:09,282
Richards: It'd sure be
nice to have some sign

32
00:01:09,284 --> 00:01:11,384
that we're not just
marching to our own deaths.

33
00:01:14,936 --> 00:01:16,436
We're not.

34
00:01:16,438 --> 00:01:18,538
Harris: Hey, tell me if you know this one.

35
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:20,506
Murphy: Not again, please.

36
00:01:20,508 --> 00:01:22,642
Harris: A Grounder and
a Reaper walk into a bar.

37
00:01:22,644 --> 00:01:25,178
The bartender looks to
the Grounder, he says,

38
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:26,646
"we don't serve your kind around here."

39
00:01:26,648 --> 00:01:28,281
The Reaper gets up and leaves.

41
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:34,120
You get it? Reapers eat Grounders.

42
00:01:34,122 --> 00:01:35,655
I will take Jaha's staff

43
00:01:35,657 --> 00:01:37,023
and beat you to death with it.

44
00:01:37,025 --> 00:01:38,891
John.

45
00:01:38,893 --> 00:01:39,826
Or this one.

46
00:01:39,828 --> 00:01:41,527
Uh, an Arker, a Grounder,

47
00:01:41,529 --> 00:01:43,563
and a Mountain Man walk into a bar.

48
00:01:43,565 --> 00:01:45,665
Arker says, "I'll take some moonshine."

49
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:47,967
Grounder says, "I'll take some, too."

50
00:01:47,969 --> 00:01:49,902
- The Mountain Man, he says...

51
00:02:04,786 --> 00:02:06,252
Aah!

53
00:02:17,732 --> 00:02:18,931
No one move!

54
00:02:20,268 --> 00:02:21,934
We're in the middle of a minefield.

55
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,039
Anybody else want a sign?

56
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:59,040
- synced and corrected by chamallow -
- www.addic7ed.com -

57
00:03:03,905 --> 00:03:06,305
Cage: It's about time, Lieutenant.

58
00:03:06,307 --> 00:03:07,773
Emerson: Yes, Sir.

59
00:03:07,775 --> 00:03:09,542
Brief me on the 44.

60
00:03:10,845 --> 00:03:11,811
I have soldiers

61
00:03:11,813 --> 00:03:13,579
going from room to room.

62
00:03:13,581 --> 00:03:15,047
It's only a matter of time.

63
00:03:15,884 --> 00:03:17,283
So, you have nothing.

64
00:03:22,156 --> 00:03:23,289
Yes, Sir.

65
00:03:24,158 --> 00:03:25,324
Those kids are the key

66
00:03:25,326 --> 00:03:27,360
to everything, Lieutenant.

67
00:03:27,362 --> 00:03:29,428
And 44 people don't just vanish

68
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:30,863
inside of a sealed bunker.

69
00:03:30,865 --> 00:03:32,665
They could if they had enough help.

70
00:03:33,668 --> 00:03:35,434
My father.

71
00:03:35,436 --> 00:03:37,403
It's unclear, Sir.

72
00:03:37,405 --> 00:03:38,571
But he's not the only one

73
00:03:38,573 --> 00:03:40,106
with moral reservations about

74
00:03:40,108 --> 00:03:41,607
what we've done to survive.

75
00:03:41,609 --> 00:03:43,109
What they don't realize is that

76
00:03:43,111 --> 00:03:44,844
those kids are dangerous.

77
00:03:44,926 --> 00:03:46,993
They irradiated an entire level.

78
00:03:46,995 --> 00:03:48,260
I agree, Sir.

79
00:03:48,262 --> 00:03:50,463
And now that level 5
has been decontaminated,

80
00:03:50,465 --> 00:03:52,431
we can tell the truth about that.

81
00:03:52,433 --> 00:03:55,801
Those kids killed 10 of our soldiers.

82
00:03:55,803 --> 00:03:57,770
We can use that to flush them out.

83
00:03:59,273 --> 00:04:00,339
Do it.

84
00:04:00,341 --> 00:04:02,475
Yes, Sir.

85
00:04:02,477 --> 00:04:04,977
Now let's talk about the outside threat.

86
00:04:04,979 --> 00:04:06,112
Look at that.

87
00:04:08,483 --> 00:04:12,251
Her entire army stopped just
outside the veil's range.

88
00:04:12,253 --> 00:04:13,519
Why?

89
00:04:13,521 --> 00:04:15,388
They're learning, Sir. I told you

90
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:16,756
this commander was different.

91
00:04:16,758 --> 00:04:19,392
What's she gonna do? Wait us out?

92
00:04:19,394 --> 00:04:22,495
We've been safe down here for 97 years.

93
00:04:22,497 --> 00:04:25,564
She's gonna lose patience,
and when she does,

94
00:04:25,566 --> 00:04:26,899
deploy the fog.

96
00:04:40,050 --> 00:04:41,416
Clarke: What if we're wrong

97
00:04:41,418 --> 00:04:43,085
and cutting the power doesn't

98
00:04:43,087 --> 00:04:45,020
disengage the locks?

99
00:04:45,022 --> 00:04:46,688
Your people said it will.

100
00:04:51,895 --> 00:04:53,495
You should rest, Clarke.

101
00:04:54,732 --> 00:04:56,398
We could blow the doors manually.

102
00:04:57,668 --> 00:04:59,768
Plans don't last very long in battle.

103
00:05:01,605 --> 00:05:04,239
Tiring yourself with questions
already asked and answered

104
00:05:04,241 --> 00:05:05,907
is a waste of energy.

105
00:05:05,909 --> 00:05:07,609
People died for this, Lexa.

106
00:05:10,948 --> 00:05:12,214
It has to work.

107
00:05:14,451 --> 00:05:16,885
You're doing what I did
when I first took command.

108
00:05:19,990 --> 00:05:21,623
We can't move forward and it's giving you

109
00:05:21,625 --> 00:05:23,625
too much time to think.

110
00:05:23,627 --> 00:05:25,093
Once Bellamy shuts down the acid fog

111
00:05:25,095 --> 00:05:26,094
and the battle begins,

112
00:05:26,096 --> 00:05:27,496
everything will be clear.

113
00:05:30,134 --> 00:05:31,399
What if he can't?

114
00:05:33,504 --> 00:05:34,736
What if it was too dangerous

115
00:05:34,738 --> 00:05:36,238
and I sent him in there anyway?

116
00:05:37,341 --> 00:05:38,640
You care about him.

117
00:05:40,344 --> 00:05:42,310
I care about all of them.

118
00:05:44,014 --> 00:05:46,281
Yet you worry about him more.

119
00:05:46,283 --> 00:05:49,117
I couldn't have kept us alive
all this time without him.

120
00:05:49,119 --> 00:05:50,318
We need him.

121
00:05:51,822 --> 00:05:54,723
And now I might be the
one who gets him killed.

122
00:05:54,725 --> 00:05:57,492
That's what it means
to be a leader, Clarke.

123
00:05:57,494 --> 00:05:58,927
The truth is, we must look into

124
00:05:58,929 --> 00:06:00,495
the eyes of our warriors and say,

125
00:06:00,497 --> 00:06:02,464
"go die for me."

126
00:06:02,466 --> 00:06:04,166
If only it were that easy.

127
00:06:05,636 --> 00:06:07,903
Can we please just get back to the plan?

128
00:06:07,905 --> 00:06:09,171
No.

129
00:06:11,008 --> 00:06:13,275
You could be a leader your people look to.

130
00:06:14,511 --> 00:06:16,945
Pour their hopes and dreams into.

131
00:06:18,816 --> 00:06:21,316
Someone they will fight and die for.

132
00:06:21,318 --> 00:06:23,451
I never asked for that.

133
00:06:25,355 --> 00:06:27,155
I'm just trying to keep us alive.

134
00:06:37,134 --> 00:06:38,967
You were born for this, Clarke.

135
00:06:41,505 --> 00:06:42,904
Same as me.

137
00:06:58,155 --> 00:07:00,755
- Raven on radio: Bellamy. Come in.

138
00:07:00,757 --> 00:07:02,757
Yeah, I'm a little busy here, Raven.

139
00:07:02,759 --> 00:07:04,092
Raven: You missed check-in.

140
00:07:04,094 --> 00:07:06,094
Did you find the source
of the acid fog yet?

141
00:07:06,096 --> 00:07:07,662
I'm making my way there now.

142
00:07:07,664 --> 00:07:10,198
It's taking longer than I thought.

143
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:12,267
I don't know enough to
crack it on this end.

144
00:07:12,269 --> 00:07:13,768
You gotta give me something.

145
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:15,070
I'm working on it.

147
00:07:18,675 --> 00:07:20,475
Something's wrong.

148
00:07:20,477 --> 00:07:21,543
Raven: What?

149
00:07:21,545 --> 00:07:23,778
My key card isn't working.

150
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:24,713
That's not good.

151
00:07:24,715 --> 00:07:27,082
I need to find another way in.

152
00:07:27,084 --> 00:07:28,950
I'll call you back.

153
00:07:28,952 --> 00:07:32,087
Stay right there! Hands in the air.

154
00:07:34,458 --> 00:07:37,192
Eastbound. In pursuit of the target.

155
00:07:37,194 --> 00:07:39,961
It's not Lovejoy. Repeat, it's not Lovejoy.

156
00:07:52,809 --> 00:07:53,975
Man: Split up.

157
00:07:57,748 --> 00:08:00,315
Garza: Checking in. We're
heading down to the base level.

158
00:08:02,052 --> 00:08:05,387
Garza: You're surrounded!
There's no way out!

159
00:08:12,095 --> 00:08:13,194
Man on radio: Keep your eyes open.

160
00:08:13,196 --> 00:08:14,496
Garza, do you see him?

161
00:08:16,433 --> 00:08:18,300
Uhh!

162
00:08:18,302 --> 00:08:19,434
Uhh!

163
00:08:22,472 --> 00:08:24,639
Man on radio: Garza, what's your status?

164
00:08:24,641 --> 00:08:26,107
Man: Garza.

165
00:08:27,978 --> 00:08:29,911
Man: Garza. Do you see him?

168
00:08:43,827 --> 00:08:46,294
I've been summoned? Really?

169
00:08:46,296 --> 00:08:48,096
Yeah. Thanks.

170
00:08:48,098 --> 00:08:50,265
I need your help on this acid fog deal.

171
00:08:50,267 --> 00:08:51,766
Bellamy will radio again when he gets

172
00:08:51,768 --> 00:08:53,001
eyes on the dispersal system,

173
00:08:53,003 --> 00:08:54,502
but I want to talk it through first.

174
00:08:54,504 --> 00:08:56,705
I think... what's funny?

175
00:08:56,707 --> 00:08:58,573
Oh, come on. It's a banner day.

176
00:08:58,575 --> 00:09:01,443
You gotta see that. Raven
Reyes asking for help?

177
00:09:01,445 --> 00:09:03,011
It's one for the history books.

178
00:09:03,013 --> 00:09:04,512
Never mind. I'll do it on my own.

179
00:09:04,514 --> 00:09:06,414
Hey. Joke.

180
00:09:06,416 --> 00:09:08,450
Humor. It's just what I do.

181
00:09:08,452 --> 00:09:10,518
There are a thousand
Grounders camped in the woods

182
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:13,355
waiting to go get my friends,

183
00:09:13,357 --> 00:09:15,190
and they can't move because...

184
00:09:16,226 --> 00:09:17,959
because I can't figure this out.

185
00:09:18,829 --> 00:09:21,162
Hey. No one could.

186
00:09:21,164 --> 00:09:23,565
It's a tough ask, not without more data.

187
00:09:27,170 --> 00:09:30,638
Ok. So, they make fog that melts people.

188
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:33,408
What are we talking? Nucleation?

189
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:36,578
Oh, please tell me it's Brownian diffusion.

190
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:38,480
I'll have you know

191
00:09:38,482 --> 00:09:40,648
I was a god at fluid dynamics.

192
00:09:40,650 --> 00:09:42,484
You think you were a god at everything.

193
00:09:44,588 --> 00:09:46,521
Empirical evidence doesn't lie.

194
00:09:51,528 --> 00:09:55,397
All right. Let's get our stoichiometry on.

196
00:10:25,162 --> 00:10:26,961
Everything ok?

197
00:10:26,963 --> 00:10:29,130
I'm going over it and over it in my head,

198
00:10:29,132 --> 00:10:32,434
just trying to figure out how

199
00:10:32,436 --> 00:10:33,935
you're still alive.

200
00:10:36,239 --> 00:10:37,806
What are you talking about?

201
00:10:37,808 --> 00:10:41,409
I saw you in Tondc before the missile hit.

202
00:10:41,411 --> 00:10:44,245
I know you, Clarke. Something's wrong.

203
00:10:44,247 --> 00:10:45,914
And then you and Lexa disappear

204
00:10:45,916 --> 00:10:47,482
and just happen to survive.

205
00:10:49,686 --> 00:10:51,453
Tell me you didn't know it was coming.

206
00:10:58,295 --> 00:10:59,661
Octavia...

207
00:11:04,901 --> 00:11:07,102
You let all those people die.

208
00:11:08,972 --> 00:11:11,106
You were gonna let me die.

209
00:11:12,109 --> 00:11:14,509
I did it to save Bellamy,

210
00:11:14,511 --> 00:11:16,411
so that we could win this war.

211
00:11:16,413 --> 00:11:18,213
Don't you see that?

212
00:11:18,215 --> 00:11:20,014
If we'd evacuated Tondc,

213
00:11:20,016 --> 00:11:21,015
Mount Weather would've known that

214
00:11:21,017 --> 00:11:22,350
someone tipped us off.

215
00:11:22,352 --> 00:11:24,119
They would have found your brother.

216
00:11:24,121 --> 00:11:26,054
No. Bellamy would have never

217
00:11:26,056 --> 00:11:27,188
told you to do that.

218
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:28,623
He would've found another way.

219
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:33,027
I couldn't take that risk.

220
00:11:33,029 --> 00:11:35,864
Right. Because you're in charge now,

221
00:11:35,866 --> 00:11:37,632
and you decide who is disposable.

222
00:11:39,970 --> 00:11:42,103
You'd have fit right in on the council.

223
00:11:45,008 --> 00:11:46,508
Hey. Octavia.

224
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:47,642
What?

225
00:11:52,415 --> 00:11:53,815
You can't tell anyone.

226
00:11:54,718 --> 00:11:55,984
If people found out...

227
00:11:55,986 --> 00:11:57,152
the alliance will break.

228
00:11:59,256 --> 00:12:00,855
I'm not an idiot, Clarke.

229
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:08,029
Commander.

230
00:12:08,031 --> 00:12:09,998
Octavia.

231
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,534
It is time for the southernmost
guard post's rotation.

232
00:12:12,536 --> 00:12:14,202
You should relieve them.

233
00:12:14,204 --> 00:12:18,006
Indra expects me to be on a
scouting mission with Lincoln.

234
00:12:18,008 --> 00:12:19,741
Now you're needed at the guard post.

235
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,043
Indra will join you there shortly.

236
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:42,931
She won't say anything.

237
00:12:42,933 --> 00:12:44,566
You can't be sure of that.

238
00:12:45,936 --> 00:12:47,702
Too many people know, Clarke.

239
00:12:49,706 --> 00:12:52,373
You worry about your people,
I'll worry about mine.

242
00:13:20,793 --> 00:13:22,392
Vincent, I need your help.

243
00:13:25,264 --> 00:13:27,264
It's all over the radio.
They know about you.

244
00:13:27,266 --> 00:13:28,465
Did anyone see you come here?

245
00:13:28,467 --> 00:13:30,000
No. Been keeping to the vents

246
00:13:30,002 --> 00:13:31,468
and unmonitored halls, like you said.

247
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:32,602
Man: Vincent.

248
00:13:34,373 --> 00:13:35,338
It's ok.

249
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:36,606
Lee's one of us.

250
00:13:36,608 --> 00:13:39,443
Dante was like a father to me.

251
00:13:39,445 --> 00:13:41,912
Some of us don't agree with Cage's agenda.

252
00:13:41,914 --> 00:13:43,180
Where's Jasper, Monty, and Maya?

253
00:13:43,182 --> 00:13:44,114
They're ok.

254
00:13:44,116 --> 00:13:45,549
Thanks to Lee, we moved them

255
00:13:45,551 --> 00:13:47,050
to a wing that's already been searched.

256
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,319
Isn't that a risk?

257
00:13:49,321 --> 00:13:50,887
We had no choice.

258
00:13:50,889 --> 00:13:53,557
They've gone public with
what happened on level 5.

259
00:13:53,559 --> 00:13:55,859
They're saying you killed 10 soldiers.

260
00:13:55,861 --> 00:13:57,194
I don't know how much longer we can

261
00:13:57,196 --> 00:13:59,129
keep this shell game going.

262
00:13:59,131 --> 00:14:01,298
Did you take out the acid fog yet?

263
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:05,001
No. No. That's why I'm here.

264
00:14:05,003 --> 00:14:06,603
I'm gonna need another route.

265
00:14:06,605 --> 00:14:07,871
Way ahead of you.

266
00:14:07,873 --> 00:14:09,206
You can get there

267
00:14:09,208 --> 00:14:11,041
through the retrofit zones.

268
00:14:13,879 --> 00:14:15,645
They're off limits.

269
00:14:15,647 --> 00:14:18,048
No cameras, no patrols.

270
00:14:18,050 --> 00:14:20,050
We use some to move the kids.

271
00:14:21,019 --> 00:14:22,786
And that's your other route.

272
00:14:22,788 --> 00:14:24,387
You're also gonna need this.

273
00:14:24,389 --> 00:14:25,856
An acetylene torch.

274
00:14:27,092 --> 00:14:29,860
Go to the northwest corridor.

276
00:14:40,205 --> 00:14:43,673
Indra. Aren't you supposed to be on watch?

277
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:45,375
I don't stand post.

278
00:14:46,545 --> 00:14:48,879
Well, um, where's Octavia?

279
00:14:48,881 --> 00:14:51,381
With Lincoln. Scouting the mountain.

280
00:15:28,453 --> 00:15:30,620
Clarke: Don't move.

281
00:15:31,957 --> 00:15:33,957
I have my orders.

282
00:15:33,959 --> 00:15:35,425
I don't care.

283
00:15:35,427 --> 00:15:37,627
This is not happening.

284
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,266
Let's go.

285
00:16:16,368 --> 00:16:17,567
Man: It's clearing.

286
00:16:37,022 --> 00:16:38,188
Murphy: There.

287
00:16:39,224 --> 00:16:41,992
We have the light and, oh, look.

288
00:16:41,994 --> 00:16:46,396
Footprints are gone. Sand. It blows.

289
00:16:53,038 --> 00:16:54,304
Do you see that?

290
00:17:02,247 --> 00:17:03,613
Richards: The City of Light.

291
00:17:04,650 --> 00:17:06,516
Emori was telling the truth.

292
00:17:09,388 --> 00:17:10,720
We are so close.

293
00:17:15,027 --> 00:17:18,194
You wanted a sign? There it is.

294
00:17:18,196 --> 00:17:20,096
We have to push forward.

295
00:17:20,098 --> 00:17:21,731
Murphy: What about the mines?

296
00:17:23,535 --> 00:17:26,369
We were meant to be here, John.

297
00:17:26,371 --> 00:17:29,673
These mines, they're just
another test of our faith.

298
00:17:31,543 --> 00:17:36,379
Yeah, well, I was always
crap at tests, so... please.

299
00:17:36,381 --> 00:17:37,747
After you, Chancellor.

300
00:17:48,827 --> 00:17:50,293
Uhh!

301
00:17:50,295 --> 00:17:52,328
Clarke: You sent him to kill Octavia?

302
00:17:52,330 --> 00:17:54,397
I told you she's not a problem.

303
00:17:57,302 --> 00:17:59,402
Leave us.

304
00:17:59,404 --> 00:18:01,705
No. I'm not letting him out of my sight.

305
00:18:04,710 --> 00:18:06,976
Stand down for now and wait for my command.

306
00:18:11,216 --> 00:18:13,016
What the hell is wrong with you?

307
00:18:13,018 --> 00:18:15,919
You can't just kill
everyone you don't trust.

308
00:18:15,921 --> 00:18:17,087
Yes, I can.

309
00:18:17,989 --> 00:18:19,422
Well, I won't let you.

310
00:18:21,359 --> 00:18:23,460
You were willing to let
her die two days ago.

311
00:18:23,462 --> 00:18:25,028
Nothing has changed.

312
00:18:25,030 --> 00:18:28,465
You're wrong. I have.

313
00:18:28,467 --> 00:18:29,933
I can't do this anymore.

314
00:18:31,903 --> 00:18:33,436
Lexa: Octavia is a threat.

315
00:18:35,574 --> 00:18:37,941
If you weren't so close
to her, you'd see that.

316
00:18:37,943 --> 00:18:40,210
It's because I'm close to her

317
00:18:40,212 --> 00:18:42,045
that I know she's loyal.

318
00:18:42,047 --> 00:18:44,914
Her brother is more
important to her than anyone.

319
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:47,283
She would never endanger his life.

320
00:18:47,285 --> 00:18:49,119
And you're willing to
risk everything on that?

321
00:18:50,856 --> 00:18:52,122
On your feelings?

322
00:18:52,124 --> 00:18:52,923
Yes.

323
00:18:53,725 --> 00:18:55,859
You say having feelings makes me weak.

324
00:18:55,861 --> 00:18:58,762
But you're weak for hiding from them.

325
00:18:58,764 --> 00:19:01,164
I might be a hypocrite,
Lexa, but you're a liar.

326
00:19:02,334 --> 00:19:04,701
You felt something for Gustus.

327
00:19:04,703 --> 00:19:07,437
You're still haunted by Costia.

328
00:19:07,439 --> 00:19:08,638
You want everyone to think

329
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,573
you're above it all,

330
00:19:09,575 --> 00:19:11,975
but I see right through you.

331
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:16,646
Get out.

332
00:19:17,683 --> 00:19:20,417
250 people died in that village.

333
00:19:20,419 --> 00:19:22,485
I know you felt for them.

334
00:19:22,487 --> 00:19:23,853
But you let them burn.

335
00:19:27,659 --> 00:19:29,159
Not everyone.

336
00:19:31,196 --> 00:19:32,462
Not you.

337
00:19:41,306 --> 00:19:45,008
Well, if you care about
me, then... trust me.

338
00:19:46,111 --> 00:19:47,677
Octavia's not a threat.

339
00:19:52,384 --> 00:19:53,516
I can't do that.

340
00:19:57,155 --> 00:19:59,189
I can't sacrifice my people anymore.

341
00:20:00,158 --> 00:20:02,726
If you do anything to hurt Octavia,

342
00:20:02,728 --> 00:20:04,995
I'll tell everyone we
knew about the missile.

343
00:20:49,782 --> 00:20:52,316
Man: There's no trap. No trap.

344
00:20:57,323 --> 00:21:00,958
It's 4 mines down, infinity to go, Jaha.

345
00:21:05,631 --> 00:21:07,030
We will make it, John.

346
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:10,367
Richards: I can't do this anymore.

347
00:21:11,337 --> 00:21:12,836
Murphy: Calm down, Richards.

348
00:21:15,407 --> 00:21:17,975
Murphy: What do you think it is, anyway?

349
00:21:17,977 --> 00:21:20,444
It must have power.

350
00:21:20,446 --> 00:21:22,679
A shower would be nice right about now.

351
00:21:22,681 --> 00:21:24,481
Wash off the rest of Harris.

353
00:21:26,852 --> 00:21:28,852
Sienna said it's a place

354
00:21:28,854 --> 00:21:31,154
where everyone is welcome.

355
00:21:31,156 --> 00:21:32,656
That'd be a first, wouldn't it?

356
00:21:35,761 --> 00:21:37,561
I can't take this. It's right there!

357
00:21:37,563 --> 00:21:39,963
Hey! Richards, stop!

358
00:21:43,569 --> 00:21:44,701
Man: Uhh!

360
00:22:39,278 --> 00:22:43,480
Hydrochloric acid. Sulfuric acid.

361
00:22:43,482 --> 00:22:46,383
Um... perchloric acid.

362
00:22:46,385 --> 00:22:49,253
Now you're just naming
all the acids you know.

363
00:22:49,255 --> 00:22:51,188
Well, temperature would be an issue.

364
00:22:51,190 --> 00:22:53,524
Hey, it could be nitric acid.

365
00:22:53,526 --> 00:22:54,992
Nothing exploded.

366
00:22:54,994 --> 00:22:56,860
Fine. Ruin my fun.

367
00:22:58,030 --> 00:22:59,530
This isn't helping.

368
00:22:59,532 --> 00:23:00,964
Like I said, we should just

369
00:23:00,966 --> 00:23:02,332
disable the machine itself.

370
00:23:02,334 --> 00:23:04,968
Any machine like this
has to have safeguards.

371
00:23:04,970 --> 00:23:06,370
They can't keep a boatload of acid around

372
00:23:06,372 --> 00:23:07,938
without any way to neutralize it.

373
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:09,706
It's basic safety protocol. Let's use that.

374
00:23:09,708 --> 00:23:11,241
Neutralization is too complicated.

375
00:23:11,243 --> 00:23:13,310
Please. It's a bag of
limestone in the corner.

376
00:23:13,312 --> 00:23:16,980
Here you go again... big
ideas with no follow-through.

377
00:23:16,982 --> 00:23:20,184
I'll have you know I
have great follow-through.

380
00:23:44,176 --> 00:23:47,277
Bellamy on radio: Come
in, Raven. I made it.

381
00:23:47,279 --> 00:23:48,712
I hope you have a plan.

382
00:23:49,582 --> 00:23:51,415
Still working on it.

383
00:23:51,417 --> 00:23:53,050
Give us something to go on.

384
00:23:53,052 --> 00:23:54,084
What do you see?

385
00:23:54,086 --> 00:23:56,954
A huge steel vat.

386
00:23:56,956 --> 00:23:58,555
Looks like a submarine.

387
00:23:58,557 --> 00:24:01,725
Some other tanks with chemical formulas

388
00:24:01,727 --> 00:24:03,861
and warning labels.

389
00:24:03,863 --> 00:24:07,598
Bunch of pipes running
into the wall. Monitor.

390
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:09,733
Ooh, go to the monitor.

391
00:24:09,735 --> 00:24:11,268
Hello to you, too.

392
00:24:11,270 --> 00:24:12,936
Don't mind Wick. He's not really helping.

393
00:24:14,139 --> 00:24:16,540
Hey, Bellamy. How's my boy Monty doing?

394
00:24:16,542 --> 00:24:18,876
Fine. But I don't know for how long.

395
00:24:18,878 --> 00:24:20,377
Great. Pleasantries over.

396
00:24:20,379 --> 00:24:22,579
Listen, if that monitor is a control panel,

397
00:24:22,581 --> 00:24:24,348
we can use it to kill this thing.

398
00:24:24,350 --> 00:24:25,716
Look for a pH scale.

399
00:24:25,718 --> 00:24:28,919
Right. It has a scale, but the rest...

400
00:24:28,921 --> 00:24:32,789
S-3, V-2-0-5,

401
00:24:32,791 --> 00:24:35,525
H-2-S-2-O-7.

402
00:24:35,527 --> 00:24:37,027
Can't I just blow this thing?

403
00:24:37,029 --> 00:24:39,096
- No.
- No, they'll know their defenses are down.

404
00:24:39,098 --> 00:24:41,131
They'll send a tech to fix it or reroute it

405
00:24:41,133 --> 00:24:43,433
or pull out some other weapon
we don't even know about.

406
00:24:43,435 --> 00:24:45,302
Plus, you'd probably melt your face off.

408
00:24:48,407 --> 00:24:50,540
Look, you know I like a good explosion,

409
00:24:50,542 --> 00:24:52,309
but we gotta think our
way through this one.

410
00:24:53,412 --> 00:24:54,611
We can do this.

411
00:24:58,183 --> 00:24:59,316
Raven: Here we go.

412
00:25:25,844 --> 00:25:27,444
Jaha: Another test passed.

413
00:25:32,651 --> 00:25:34,551
We made it.

414
00:25:34,553 --> 00:25:35,719
Come on.

415
00:25:54,807 --> 00:25:56,340
Are you kidding me?

416
00:25:57,609 --> 00:25:59,643
Are you kidding me? This is it?

417
00:26:07,653 --> 00:26:09,853
Murphy: This is what we
crossed a desert to find?

418
00:26:12,291 --> 00:26:14,491
It can't be.

419
00:26:14,493 --> 00:26:16,626
Well, guess what? Your enlightened society?

420
00:26:16,628 --> 00:26:19,062
It's not a city. It's nothing.

421
00:26:20,733 --> 00:26:22,466
I flew down from space.

422
00:26:26,038 --> 00:26:27,471
I defied death.

423
00:26:28,540 --> 00:26:29,873
It was all for a reason.

424
00:26:32,177 --> 00:26:33,377
It has to be.

425
00:26:41,695 --> 00:26:43,662
Ok, uh... Level indicator.

426
00:26:44,531 --> 00:26:45,730
Nope.

427
00:26:47,167 --> 00:26:49,868
Do you see an actuator anywhere?

428
00:26:49,870 --> 00:26:51,336
One must be controlling the valves.

429
00:26:52,940 --> 00:26:54,940
I have no idea what that is.

430
00:26:55,876 --> 00:26:59,444
Norms. Come on, what else?

431
00:26:59,446 --> 00:27:01,480
Internal pressure sensor.

432
00:27:01,482 --> 00:27:02,647
No.

433
00:27:02,649 --> 00:27:04,883
Uh, setpoint and alarm.

434
00:27:04,885 --> 00:27:07,052
Let's avoid that one.

435
00:27:07,054 --> 00:27:08,987
Maintenance and cleaning.

436
00:27:08,989 --> 00:27:10,155
Wait.

437
00:27:11,391 --> 00:27:12,791
Corrosion.

438
00:27:12,793 --> 00:27:14,125
The protective oxide film would

439
00:27:14,127 --> 00:27:16,094
have to be restored in tanks this old.

440
00:27:16,096 --> 00:27:17,496
They'd need to be cleaned.

441
00:27:17,498 --> 00:27:18,864
And neutralized.

442
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,466
Bellamy, go to that subdirectory.

443
00:27:21,468 --> 00:27:23,768
See if there's anything
there that says "passivation."

444
00:27:25,439 --> 00:27:27,105
- Ok. I'm on it.

446
00:27:29,109 --> 00:27:30,976
Got it.

448
00:27:32,579 --> 00:27:36,348
Says, uh, "aqueous sodium hydroxide bath."

449
00:27:36,350 --> 00:27:38,984
That's a base. That'll
neutralize the acid. Select that.

451
00:27:43,524 --> 00:27:47,726
It's doing something.

452
00:27:47,728 --> 00:27:50,128
Raven: You should be able to hear the pump.

453
00:27:50,130 --> 00:27:51,496
Bellamy: I can hear them.

454
00:27:55,035 --> 00:27:56,234
Needle's moving.

455
00:27:57,337 --> 00:28:00,305
- Bellamy: pH is rising.
- It's working.

457
00:28:14,922 --> 00:28:16,655
Passivation success.

458
00:28:16,657 --> 00:28:19,024
- Both: Yes!

459
00:28:22,129 --> 00:28:24,362
Bellamy: All right. Send a flare.

460
00:28:26,900 --> 00:28:28,033
Roger that.

461
00:28:34,174 --> 00:28:35,540
You sent for me?

462
00:28:37,344 --> 00:28:38,476
Yes.

463
00:28:39,780 --> 00:28:41,947
Octavia has nothing to fear from me.

464
00:28:45,886 --> 00:28:48,153
I do trust you, Clarke.

465
00:28:50,691 --> 00:28:52,891
I know how hard that is for you.

466
00:28:58,699 --> 00:29:02,100
You think our ways are harsh,

467
00:29:02,102 --> 00:29:03,868
but that's how we survive.

468
00:29:04,671 --> 00:29:06,204
Maybe life should be about

469
00:29:06,206 --> 00:29:08,373
more than just surviving.

470
00:29:10,043 --> 00:29:11,876
Don't we deserve better than that?

471
00:29:15,916 --> 00:29:17,315
Maybe we do.

472
00:29:42,275 --> 00:29:43,708
I'm sorry. I...

473
00:29:45,479 --> 00:29:48,413
I'm not ready... to be with anyone.

474
00:29:52,085 --> 00:29:53,418
Not yet.

475
00:30:00,119 --> 00:30:01,946
_

476
00:30:02,647 --> 00:30:04,112
_

477
00:30:13,140 --> 00:30:14,572
Bellamy did it.

478
00:30:16,777 --> 00:30:18,743
You were right to have faith in him.

479
00:30:23,116 --> 00:30:24,449
Now we fight.

486
00:31:00,153 --> 00:31:02,687
When I said, "let's get our
stoichiometry on," not what I meant.

487
00:31:09,730 --> 00:31:13,231
Ah. Um, it's probably a bad idea.

488
00:31:13,233 --> 00:31:15,700
We're going to war. Stop talking.

490
00:31:35,388 --> 00:31:37,756
I'm just saying, the brace I made

491
00:31:37,758 --> 00:31:39,124
would've been easier to take off.

492
00:31:41,061 --> 00:31:42,727
That brace was tragic.

493
00:31:43,830 --> 00:31:45,630
What did I say about talking, Wick?

494
00:31:46,700 --> 00:31:48,566
I think you can call me Kyle.


497
00:32:58,159 --> 00:32:59,925
Raven, we've got a problem.

498
00:33:01,562 --> 00:33:03,796
Bellamy on radio: Dammit, where are you?

499
00:33:03,798 --> 00:33:05,464
I don't think the acid fog is down.

500
00:33:05,466 --> 00:33:09,568
Get word to Clarke. We have
to stop the army. Raven!

501
00:33:09,570 --> 00:33:12,304
Confirmed, Sir. Intruder's
radio has been cut off.

502
00:33:12,306 --> 00:33:14,206
Bellamy: Raven, what's going on?

503
00:33:14,208 --> 00:33:15,775
Reset the panel.

504
00:33:16,911 --> 00:33:18,677
The army's almost in range.

506
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:27,186
Oh.

507
00:33:27,188 --> 00:33:29,054
Good job finding the radio, Lieutenant.

508
00:33:30,391 --> 00:33:32,458
Do a sweep and make sure they have no more.

509
00:33:32,460 --> 00:33:33,426
Yes, Sir.

510
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:35,661
And bring me the intruder.

512
00:33:50,178 --> 00:33:51,777
Drop your weapon!

514
00:34:04,459 --> 00:34:06,559
Garza: On my lead.

515
00:34:06,561 --> 00:34:08,327
He's armed. Don't be a hero.

516
00:34:11,299 --> 00:34:14,300
Show yourself. Hands first.

517
00:34:17,839 --> 00:34:20,506
Cease fire! Don't hit the tanks.

519
00:34:32,787 --> 00:34:35,321
The veil is ready on your command, Sir.

520
00:34:35,323 --> 00:34:38,057
Wait until they're all
inside at the kill box.

521
00:34:38,059 --> 00:34:39,425
10 more seconds.

522
00:34:39,427 --> 00:34:41,827
Emerson: Roger that. Deploying in 10...

523
00:34:43,064 --> 00:34:44,530
9...

524
00:34:46,601 --> 00:34:49,168
- 8…

525
00:34:49,170 --> 00:34:50,202
7...

526
00:34:50,204 --> 00:34:51,704
He's out.

527
00:34:51,706 --> 00:34:53,706
Man: You go after him.
We'll check the tanks.

528
00:34:53,708 --> 00:34:56,842
Emerson: 6... 5...

529
00:34:58,079 --> 00:34:59,378
4...

530
00:35:01,482 --> 00:35:02,648
3...

531
00:35:04,819 --> 00:35:07,019
2... 1.

533
00:35:08,756 --> 00:35:10,055
We're go for veil.

537
00:35:57,104 --> 00:35:58,904
Well?

538
00:35:58,906 --> 00:36:01,307
We are negative on veil deployment.

539
00:36:01,309 --> 00:36:02,908
What happened?

540
00:36:02,910 --> 00:36:05,744
Soldiers report an explosion
in chemicals deployment.

541
00:36:05,746 --> 00:36:07,846
Multiple casualties.

542
00:36:07,848 --> 00:36:09,915
The veil is down. I
repeat, the veil is down.

543
00:36:09,917 --> 00:36:11,383
What else can we use?

544
00:36:11,385 --> 00:36:13,652
The Reapers can't take a force this large.

545
00:36:13,654 --> 00:36:15,921
Don't tell me what we can't do.

546
00:36:15,923 --> 00:36:17,723
Tell me what else we have.

547
00:36:19,927 --> 00:36:23,028
Nothing. All we have is the doors.

548
00:37:00,481 --> 00:37:01,613
Hey.

549
00:37:04,852 --> 00:37:06,485
We have to meet the strike team.

550
00:37:08,822 --> 00:37:12,891
You kind of, ahem, shut
down on me there. What's up?

551
00:37:14,862 --> 00:37:16,662
What?

552
00:37:16,664 --> 00:37:17,796
Nothing.

553
00:37:22,036 --> 00:37:23,502
Right.

554
00:37:25,172 --> 00:37:26,505
This was too much.

555
00:37:33,681 --> 00:37:34,813
Look...

556
00:37:37,017 --> 00:37:38,617
If you want to do this, I'm in.

557
00:37:40,521 --> 00:37:42,154
But I'm not gonna play games.

558
00:37:42,156 --> 00:37:43,321
So, figure it out.

559
00:37:52,733 --> 00:37:54,132
We have a war to win.

561
00:38:21,028 --> 00:38:22,160
Hey.

562
00:38:23,897 --> 00:38:25,063
What do you want?

563
00:38:27,267 --> 00:38:28,700
I'm changing your mission.

564
00:38:28,702 --> 00:38:30,936
You're not going to the mines with Indra.

565
00:38:30,938 --> 00:38:32,671
I'm placing you in the rear guard,

566
00:38:32,673 --> 00:38:34,206
where you'll be safe.

567
00:38:34,208 --> 00:38:36,441
Like hell you are. I
don't take orders from you.

568
00:38:36,443 --> 00:38:37,943
I take orders from Indra.

569
00:38:37,945 --> 00:38:39,711
I'm trying to protect you, Octavia.

570
00:38:39,713 --> 00:38:41,880
Protect me.

571
00:38:41,882 --> 00:38:44,216
One day, hopefully, you'll
understand what I did.

572
00:38:44,218 --> 00:38:46,585
Never. I'll fight this war with you now

573
00:38:46,587 --> 00:38:48,887
because I want our friends back.

574
00:38:48,889 --> 00:38:50,222
But after that, we're done.

575
00:38:56,396 --> 00:38:58,096
The commander's looking for you.

576
00:39:01,802 --> 00:39:03,735
What was that about?

577
00:39:03,737 --> 00:39:05,737
Clarke's trying to reassign
me to the rear guard.

578
00:39:06,640 --> 00:39:07,906
You're a warrior.

579
00:39:07,908 --> 00:39:09,307
You'll be in the mines with me.

580
00:39:10,744 --> 00:39:12,644
I know what bothers you.

581
00:39:12,646 --> 00:39:14,646
They know about the missile.

582
00:39:14,648 --> 00:39:16,448
How could you not hate them?

583
00:39:16,450 --> 00:39:17,783
Indra, they almost killed you.

584
00:39:17,785 --> 00:39:20,652
They didn't do anything. The enemy did.

585
00:39:20,654 --> 00:39:23,855
Lexa's a great commander
because she's ruthless.

586
00:39:23,857 --> 00:39:25,524
That's why we'll win this battle.

587
00:39:25,526 --> 00:39:26,958
That's wrong.

588
00:39:26,960 --> 00:39:28,927
That's war.

589
00:39:28,929 --> 00:39:31,129
- Yaaah!

590
00:39:38,172 --> 00:39:40,338
Yaaah!

591
00:39:55,322 --> 00:39:57,055
What a joke.

592
00:40:00,527 --> 00:40:02,194
Jaha: It doesn't make any sense.

593
00:40:02,196 --> 00:40:04,863
The rest of the world is broken,

594
00:40:04,865 --> 00:40:06,832
but these panels are intact.

595
00:40:06,834 --> 00:40:08,366
Well, we can fix that.

596
00:40:09,970 --> 00:40:12,003
- Jaha: John.

597
00:40:19,379 --> 00:40:20,612
What the hell is that?

598
00:40:23,116 --> 00:40:24,716
It's a drone.

599
00:40:24,718 --> 00:40:26,117
Jaha: Don't lose sight of it.

600
00:40:45,672 --> 00:40:46,705
Where's it going?

601
00:40:46,707 --> 00:40:47,806
I don't know...

602
00:40:48,742 --> 00:40:50,108
but we're gonna follow it.

603
00:40:50,110 --> 00:40:52,143
In this.

604
00:40:52,145 --> 00:40:55,146
Tell me, what level of
crazy is too much for you?

605
00:40:55,148 --> 00:40:56,414
I'm just curious.

606
00:40:59,720 --> 00:41:04,022
We need a boat... and a boat appears.

607
00:41:04,024 --> 00:41:05,423
This is our destiny.

608
00:41:06,360 --> 00:41:07,726
The City of Light is out there

609
00:41:07,728 --> 00:41:09,027
and we are gonna find it.

610
00:41:10,430 --> 00:41:11,763
Now, get in the boat.

611
00:41:16,436 --> 00:41:17,836
You heard the man.
 
